## Purpose

Mugheer exists so that a client never has to email a project manager to ask "how's it going?" or "is my site still up?". In one dashboard, a client can request a product, watch it get designed and built, launch it, monitor it live, configure automation around it, and pay for all of it. Internally, the same platform is how our engineers, designers, and admins run the business: assigning work, tracking delivery, responding to alerts, and reviewing what our AI systems are doing on our behalf.

Full product specification, architecture rationale, and build brief: see [`docs/MUGHEER_MASTER_PROMPT.md`](docs/MUGHEER_MASTER_PROMPT.md).

## Architecture Overview

Mugheer is built as a strict **three-tier architecture**:

```
[ Browser / Mobile Client ]
        |  HTTPS (REST/GraphQL, WebSocket)
        v
[ Tier 1: Frontend — React SPA behind CloudFront/Nginx ]
        |  HTTPS (internal ALB)
        v
[ Tier 2: Application Layer ]
   Auth · Projects · Billing · Monitoring · Automation · AI Orchestration
        |
        v
[ Tier 3: Data Layer ]
   PostgreSQL · Redis · S3 · Prometheus/Timescale
```

The frontend never talks to the database directly. Only the application layer talks to the data layer. This is enforced both in code and at the network level (Kubernetes NetworkPolicies, AWS security groups).

See [`docs/ARCHITECTURE.md`](docs/ARCHITECTURE.md) for the full diagram and reasoning.

